# Line endings are pinned here rather than left to whatever the machine prefers.
#
# The bundled CSVs in backend/app/data/ are the reason this file exists.
# docs/05-DATA-AND-PIPELINE.md requires them to be byte-reproducible, and a test
# regenerates them and asserts the result matches the committed file exactly.
# Git's Windows default, core.autocrlf=true, rewrites them to CRLF on checkout:
# one extra byte per line, 12,848 of them in orders.csv. That fails the test on
# every fresh clone on Windows while passing on the machine that generated the
# files, because those were written by Python and never checked out again. It is
# invisible until somebody else clones the repository.
#
# Everything else is LF for the same reason it is worth having one answer at
# all: this repository was authored with LF, and a working tree that differs by
# platform is a difference nobody chose.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Redundant under the rule above, and kept anyway so the constraint is written
# down next to the thing it protects.
backend/app/data/*.csv text eol=lf
